# Key columns whose types cannot be compared are DS2003.
mode: check
show: schema
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, timestamp: datetime); 'r.csv'(customerId: long, qty: string)
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | join 'r.csv' on customerId;
from 'orders.csv' | join 'r.csv' on $left.qty == $right.qty
---- expected
error[DS2003]: cannot join on `customerId`: the left side is `string` and the right side is `long`
  --> query:1:37
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | join 'r.csv' on customerId;
  |                                     ^^^^^^^^^^ the key columns have types that cannot be compared
  |
  = help: convert the right column first: `join (from 'r.csv' | extend customerId = tostring(customerId)) on customerId`
  = note: on the left `customerId` is `string` (read from orders.csv); on the right `customerId` is `long` (read from r.csv)

error[DS2003]: cannot join on `$left.qty` and `$right.qty`: the left side is `long` and the right side is `string`
  --> query:2:37
  |
2 | from 'orders.csv' | join 'r.csv' on $left.qty == $right.qty
  |                                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the key columns have types that cannot be compared
  |
  = help: convert the right column first: `join (from 'r.csv' | extend qty = tolong(qty)) on $left.qty == $right.qty`
  = note: on the left `qty` is `long` (read from orders.csv); on the right `qty` is `string` (read from r.csv)

query 1 columns:
  orderId: string
  customerId: (error)
  amount: real
  qty: long
  timestamp: datetime
  qty1: string

query 2 columns:
  orderId: string
  customerId: string
  amount: real
  qty: long
  timestamp: datetime
  customerId1: long
  qty1: string
